Subject: [PATCH] debayer: import the IMX362 packed input through an aligned R8 view

The walleye VFE writes 2520 bytes per line. fd5 linear R8 needs a
64-byte pitch. Use a 3136x1215 view only for the matching packed RAW10
configuration and buffers large enough for 1216 physical rows. Translate
each logical byte in the fragment shader. Preserve the original upload
layout per frame and keep CPU statistics on the camera stride.

Downstream candidate for libcamera v0.7.1 with postmarketOS patch 0003.
Remove when upstream handles this fd5 input layout and same-frame output
and import counters have been verified on walleye.

